body: |-
  METHOD: five-agent adversarial audit (each tasked to FALSIFY) → founder picked Track A (harden the instrument) → 6 findings fixed (2 by me on the interlocking native/admit files, 2+ by parallel builder subagents on disjoint files, 1 protocol doc by architect) → consolidated single-threaded full suite → pre-commit reviewer pass → fixed the 2 findings the review surfaced → commit. The concurrent-worker 60s test timeouts were CPU oversubscription, NOT regressions (confirmed: clean single-threaded).

  WHAT'S DONE (committed b85d56a8):
  - B-1: proposeNative seals byte-custody strand on meaning-NOOP+tree-advance; admitNative NOOP branch carries it as FAST_ADMIT when it linearly fast-forwards the selvage. Held (not lost) under concurrent meaning advance.
  - B-3: persistContested() helper on both contested sites; downgrade sets rebasedOnto:=selvage.stateId (fixes the FAST_ADMIT-flavor silent throw B-1 made reachable); payloadError field + CLI render.
  - I-1: findKnotPayloadForResolve unconditional+deterministic; C-9 loud guard in resolve.
  - I-2: printAdmit renders derivedStale.
  - hazard-forecast: evaluateHazards wired into oracle()/weave --preview, advisory-only.
  - 4 new tests; full suite 1023/115/exit 0.

  STILL OPEN (tracked, NOT in this commit):
  - T-2026-08-11-018 field-test protocol — DRAFTED, awaits FOUNDER review (n=100 fixed, contested floor=20, green-gate+behavioral-smoke false-CLEAN oracle, blinded 2nd rater that also discharges the LLM-judge falsifier T-2026-07-14-004).
  - T-2026-08-11-019 git-era B-3 arm (admit.ts:1006/1043 same downgrade gap; off the native field-test path).
  - Judge follow-ups (not yet ticketed): contentless byte-conflict payload (contested:[] — thread mat.plan.conflicts in); BYTE_ADMIT status/flag for legibility (byte-custody carry currently relabels to FAST_ADMIT with empty agentChanged).
  - T-2026-08-11-020 teaching-surface refresh (university + notebooks + docs) — GATED on interface finalization.
  - The 28+ unpushed commits: push STILL never authorized.

  WHAT TRACK A DID NOT DO (deliberately — these are the OTHER tracks, still not-ready for the product claim): the meaning judge is still never validated against a real model (T-2026-07-14-004 partially discharged only IF the protocol's blinded-LLM-rater is built); the security boundary is still one unsigned env var (M3); no publishing, branching, cold-model, GUI migration. Track A makes the FIELD TEST honest; it does not make the PRODUCT CLAIM true.
